    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 16-layer planar dielectric stack on silicon substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2 (16 finite layers total). Initialize all HfO2 layers at quarter-wave optical thickness for 10500 nm central wavelength, initialize all SiO2 layers at quarter-wave optical thickness for 10500 nm. Apply ±8% thickness bounds around initial values during optimization. Target: maximize mean absorptance in 8000-13000 nm band, minimize mean absorptance in 3000-5000 nm band. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized or both TE/TM. Materials: HfO2 and SiO2 from material registry with IR refractive index data. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3000-5000 nm, 8000-13000 nm. soft objectives: high emissivity in 8000-13000 nm; low emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 24.",
